filebrowser/--datasheet--                       filebrowser/--datasheet--

    NAME
	FileBrowser -- listbrowser.gadget subclass with an icon (cell)
	view mode. (1.1)

    SUPERCLASS
	listbrowser.gadget

    DESCRIPTION
	FileBrowser is a ListBrowser that can also show its list as icons.
	It is not a library: add FileBrowser.c to your program's build and
	include FileBrowser.h. The class is private, so objects are made
	with the class pointer that MakeFileBrowserClass() returns:

	    Object *gad = NewObject(cl, NULL, ...tags..., TAG_DONE);

	FBVM_DETAILS (the default view mode): every method goes to
	listbrowser.gadget, so the gadget looks and behaves exactly like a
	ListBrowser. A program can replace its ListBrowser with a
	FileBrowser and nothing changes for the user.

	FBVM_ICONS: each list node is drawn as a cell: its image (or a full
	size icon from the program, see FILEBROWSER_IconHook) on top, then
	one line of text per list column. All cells have the same width and
	flow left to right, top to bottom, using as many cell columns as fit
	the gadget. The view only scrolls vertically; a scroll bar is shown
	on the right when the cells don't fit. Texts longer than the cell
	are cropped as "Long str...".

	Switching the view is one attribute; the list, the column info and
	the program's event handling stay as they are:

	    SetGadgetAttrs(gad, win, NULL,
	                   FILEBROWSER_ViewMode, FBVM_ICONS, TAG_DONE);

    REQUIREMENTS
	AmigaOS 4.1. The class uses the global interface pointers of the
	program: IExec, IIntuition, IGraphics, ILayers, IUtility, IIcon and
	IListBrowser must be valid before MakeFileBrowserClass() is called
	and while any FileBrowser object exists.

    METHODS
	OM_NEW, OM_DISPOSE -- Passed to the superclass; the class data for
	    icon mode is set up and freed.

	OM_SET, OM_UPDATE -- FILEBROWSER_* attributes are handled here.
	    Everything is also passed to listbrowser.gadget; in icon mode
	    without a GadgetInfo, so it keeps its state but doesn't draw.

	OM_GET -- FILEBROWSER_* attributes are answered here, everything
	    else by listbrowser.gadget. In icon mode the selection
	    attributes (see NOTES) come from the icon view.

	GM_RENDER, GM_HITTEST, GM_GOACTIVE, GM_HANDLEINPUT,
	GM_HANDLESCROLL, GM_GOINACTIVE -- Handled here in icon mode, passed
	    to listbrowser.gadget in details mode.

	All other methods are passed to listbrowser.gadget.

    ATTRIBUTES
	All LISTBROWSER_* attributes work as with listbrowser.gadget. The
	class adds:

	FILEBROWSER_ViewMode (uint32)
	    FBVM_DETAILS: the plain ListBrowser view.
	    FBVM_ICONS: the icon (cell) view.

	    Defaults to FBVM_DETAILS.

	    Applicability is (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

	FILEBROWSER_CellChars (uint32)
	    Width of a cell in characters of the gadget's font. The cell
	    also grows to fit the widest image or icon.

	    Defaults to 14.

	    Applicability is (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

	FILEBROWSER_HiddenColumns (uint32)
	    Bit mask of list columns that are not shown in the cells (bit n
	    = column n), for the whole gadget. Columns that have no text
	    (LBNCA_Text) in the first node are never shown.

	    Defaults to 0: every column is shown.

	    Applicability is (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

	FILEBROWSER_BackgroundPen (int32)
	    Pen used to fill the background in icon mode.

	    Defaults to -1: the background pen of the first node (when the
	    list uses custom pens), else BACKGROUNDPEN.

	    Applicability is (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

	FILEBROWSER_IconHook (struct Hook *)
	    Icon mode: a hook that returns a full size icon for a node,
	    drawn instead of the node's LBNCA_Image. Called as

	        icon = (struct DiskObject *)CallHookPkt(hook, gadget, node);

	    It returns a struct DiskObject * owned by the program that stays
	    valid while the node is in the list, or NULL to draw the node's
	    LBNCA_Image. The hook can be called from input.device while
	    rendering, so it must not do any DOS I/O: load the icons
	    beforehand or in the background, and refresh the gadget when
	    they are ready.

	    Defaults to NULL: the nodes' images are drawn.

	    Applicability is (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

	FILEBROWSER_IconSize (uint32)
	    Icon mode: the size in pixels of the image box of every cell,
	    like an icon grid. Icons from FILEBROWSER_IconHook that are
	    larger are drawn scaled down to fit, keeping their aspect ratio;
	    smaller ones are drawn at their original size, bottom aligned.
	    icon.library caches the scaled imagery in each icon.

	    With a fixed box the cells keep their size while icons load in
	    the background (the node's LBNCA_Image is drawn until the hook
	    returns an icon) or when icons change.

	    Defaults to 0: no fixed box. Every icon is drawn at its original
	    size and the box is as large as the largest image or icon shown.

	    Applicability is (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

    NOTES
	In icon mode these ListBrowser attributes keep working, and
	selections carry over when the view mode changes:
	LISTBROWSER_Selected, LISTBROWSER_SelectedNode,
	LISTBROWSER_NumSelected, LISTBROWSER_RelEvent, LISTBROWSER_Top,
	LISTBROWSER_MakeVisible, LISTBROWSER_Position,
	LISTBROWSER_MultiSelect, LISTBROWSER_PersistSelect and
	LISTBROWSER_TotalNodes.

	Mouse in icon mode:
	 - A click selects a cell. With LISTBROWSER_MultiSelect, Shift
	   toggles a cell's selection.
	 - A double-click sends LBRE_DOUBLECLICK, as in details mode.
	 - Dragging from empty space draws a selection box (lasso) that
	   selects the cells inside it; it follows the pointer anywhere in
	   the view. With Shift it adds to the selection.
	 - Dragging from a cell leaves the selection alone, so the program's
	   own drag & drop works as in details mode. Pressing on a cell of a
	   multiple selection keeps the selection; releasing without moving
	   narrows it to that cell.
	 - The mouse wheel scrolls the view.

	The cells are drawn into an offscreen bitmap and blitted in one go,
	so scrolling doesn't flicker. Without memory for the buffer they are
	drawn directly, clipped to the gadget.

    BUGS
	Not done yet in icon mode: column titles (for sorting), per column
	text justification in the cells, keyboard navigation, and
	hierarchical lists (LBNA_Generation) are not supported.

    SEE ALSO
	gadgets/listbrowser.gadget, icon.library/DrawIconStateA(),
	MakeFileBrowserClass(), FreeFileBrowserClass(), FileBrowserDemo.c

filebrowser/FreeFileBrowserClass               filebrowser/FreeFileBrowserClass

    NAME
	FreeFileBrowserClass -- Free the FileBrowser class. (1.0)

    SYNOPSIS
	void FreeFileBrowserClass(struct IClass *cl);

    FUNCTION
	Frees a class made by MakeFileBrowserClass(). Call it only after
	every object made from the class has been disposed (a window object
	disposes its gadgets).

    INPUTS
	cl - the class pointer, NULL is allowed.

    SEE ALSO
	MakeFileBrowserClass()

filebrowser/MakeFileBrowserClass               filebrowser/MakeFileBrowserClass

    NAME
	MakeFileBrowserClass -- Create the FileBrowser class. (1.0)

    SYNOPSIS
	struct IClass *cl = MakeFileBrowserClass(void);

    FUNCTION
	Creates the private FileBrowser class, a subclass of
	listbrowser.gadget. Make objects with NewObject(cl, NULL, ...).

	IExec, IIntuition, IGraphics, ILayers, IUtility, IIcon and
	IListBrowser must be open first.

    RESULT
	cl - the class, or NULL if it could not be made.

    EXAMPLE
	struct IClass *cl = MakeFileBrowserClass();
	if(cl)
	{
	    Object *gad = NewObject(cl, NULL,
	        GA_ID,                    GID_FILES,
	        GA_RelVerify,             TRUE,
	        LISTBROWSER_Labels,       &list,
	        LISTBROWSER_ColumnInfo,   columninfo,
	        LISTBROWSER_ColumnTitles, TRUE,
	        LISTBROWSER_MultiSelect,  TRUE,
	        FILEBROWSER_ViewMode,     FBVM_ICONS,
	        FILEBROWSER_IconSize,     64,
	        TAG_DONE);
	    ...
	    DisposeObject(windowobject);  /* disposes gad too */
	    FreeFileBrowserClass(cl);
	}

    SEE ALSO
	FreeFileBrowserClass()

